  str_aircraft_tactic_info11101 = "Gold River: Originating in the World's Spine, it is the longest river in all of Astra. It is supplemented by the melting snow covering the mountains of its origin and winds throughout the entire continent.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11102 = "Livelihoods Along the Gold River: The villages dotting the Gold River basin owe their prosperity to the Gold River's flowing waters and fertile banks. The river's main course is lined with well-developed villages that rely on advanced communications and robust trade to improve their settlements.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11103 = "Village Cuisine: Villagers along the Gold River frequently consume peas and pea products, marinated fish, and animal meats. These are the easiest and most readily-accessible foods for them to acquire.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11104 = "Commerce: Many Gold River merchants work along strictly-established trade routes, peddling their wares up and down the prosperous cities that line its banks.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11201 = "The Gold River: The Gold River stretches endlessly across the land from the sky, running from the northwest to the southeast and, finally, flowing into the sea.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11202 = "Livelihoods Along the Gold River: The villages near the Gold River's tributaries still adhere to more traditional modes of life, where villagers either subsist by fishing or irrigating their farms with its waters.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11203 = "Village Cuisine: The villagers also grow wheat to a certain extent, but it is seldom eaten. Instead, it is used to brew beer, which is indispensable to many locals.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11204 = "Commerce: When presented with unique opportunities, a few merchants may be willing to open new trade routes across the land. Naturally, given the unfamiliar and risky state of affairs in the world, they are almost always escorted by armed guards.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11301 = "Luminatics: Not all Aurorians are born with the ability to wield Luminatics. It is more like a kind of potential waiting to be activated.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11302 = "Lumopolis Ration: A standard ration for Lumopolis soldiers, made of white bread enriched with appropriate salt and sugar and blended with Luminatics.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11303 = "Plate Armor: Body armor worn by knights and provided by the church. Most knights are equipped with heavy but more defensive plate armor, and certain knights value mobility over the defense and equip themselves with chain mail.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11304 = "Tower Shield: An iconic and indispensable piece of Lumo Knight equipment, it represents the knightly order of Lumopolis. The shape and size of the shield may vary slightly depending on the soldier wielding it, but the coat of arms it bears on its surface remains unchanged.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11401 = "Luminatics: Can be activated by various causes. A certain person's guidance, a crucial moment in a person's history... Many Aurorians live their entire lives without ever using Luminatics, but the light of the sun shines upon them all the same.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11402 = "Lumopolis Ration: This ration not only has a longer shelf life, it also tastes better. Light, easy to carry, with great balance of sweet and salty. This military ration is meant to satisfy hunger, but it is still better than most food available to the common folk.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11403 = "Plate Armor: Some knights would choose custom-made armor. In certain combat situations, there are even knights who will opt to wear different types of armor all at once.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11404 = "Tower Shield: The church will award the shield to the knights on the day they were inducted into the order, it symbolizes Lumopolis' belief that protection is far more important than conquest. The shield is seen as more powerful than the sword and is synonymous with chivalry and duty.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11501 = "The Courier Union: A postal service organization that has existed for centuries. Despite its small number of members, it receives widespread acclaim throughout Astra for its extremely fast and efficient deliveries.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11502 = "Posts: Facilities unique to the Courier Union serve as resting places for its couriers and provide food and other supplies required on their journeys. People who wish to have letters delivered can drop them off here as well.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11503 = "Itineraries: These notebooks record a courier's travels while out on deliveries.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11504 = "Dandelion: A special flower symbolizing Eraveil, it was beloved by all Caelestites for its white and fluffy appearance, as well as its representation of unbridled freedom.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11601 = "The Courier Union: The Courier Union is often contracted for long-distance deliveries across borders, sometimes through dangerous routes closed off to the public.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11602 = "Posts: There are also mailboxes at the entrance of these Posts. Those who wish to have letters delivered can drop them off here, and the next courier who arrives at the Post will receive it for delivery.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11603 = "Itineraries: Couriers record the letters they have delivered or are currently delivering, the Posts at which they stop to rest, and so on. Arguably the most important personal effect of any courier.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11604 = "Dandelions: Despite their abundance inside Eraveil, the Caelestites were fond of creating objects and decorations in their image during their holidays.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11701 = "Azurite: An enormous floating island hovering over the Astra Plain. Many years ago, the Aurorians of the distant north struggled against both their homeland's inhospitable environment and the ever-present Eclipsite threat. Leaving their home behind, they arrived in Astra and eventually found a way to climb atop Azurite.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11702 = "The Shuttle Hub: The Shuttle Hub in Lower Lumopolis is the only port of entry for the entire city. All airships traveling in and out of Lumopolis must pass this place and be subject to stringent inspections regardless of the direction of travel. In many cases, applications must be made well in advance to pass through this port.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11703 = "Umbraton and Azurite: As the city-state closest to Azurite, Umbraton is a natural conduit between Lumopolis and the outside world.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11704 = "Airships: The main method of transportation to and from Lumopolis. Depending on their manufacturing site, different airships can possess not only different appearances but different propulsion systems, as well. An example of these differences is the airships manufactured in Illumina, which are industrial design and driven by heat. Lumopolis airships, on the other hand, focus more on outward beauty and elegance and are powered by Lumina.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11801 = "Azurite: Aurorians established a society with the nobility at the core, a social order based on an ancient imperial system. Thus was the island of Azurite transformed into Lumopolis—the grand, floating city in the sky.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11802 = "Shuttle Hubs: The Shuttle Hub is divided into four sectors, each with its specified type of traffic: tourism, logistical, military, and special.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11803 = "Umbraton and Azurite: An airship port for entry and exit into Lumopolis has been established here under the sole jurisdiction of Lumopolis. In the majority of instances, one must pass through Umbraton to enter Azurite.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11804 = "Airships: The ports of Umbraton and Lumopolis provide airships as a means of public transportation for their citizenry. Some prominent and wealthy citizens even have their private airships.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11901 = "Courier's Badge: A badge engraved with a writing quill on its surface. A valuable token that proves the wearer's identity as a member of the Courier Union, it is usually seen hanging from a courier's itinerary.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11902 = "Lower Lumopolis: The city's center of agricultural and industrial production. Relatively tiny residential space, but its population density is the highest in all of Lumopolis.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11903 = "Inside the Shuttle Hub: The most vibrant and bustling hub of commercial activity in all of Lumopolis. Here, you can find all manner of people—merchants and nobles waiting for airships, also tourists with heavy coin purses.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info11904 = "Commodities of Lumopolis: Mainly dealing in luxury goods, things in Lumopolis generally include gold and silver jewelry, precious gemstones, and exquisite furs.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info12001 = "Courier's Badge: Each Post carries several spare badges, in case an absent-minded courier manages to lose their own.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info12002 = "Lower Lumopolis: This is the home to the lower-class nobility, as well as the servants of the middle and upper-class nobles. It is a veritable melting pot of the urban and the rural, especially when compared to the Lumopolis Gardens or the Lumopolis Courtyard.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info12003 = "Shuttle Hubs: Sharp-eyed vendors have found the opportunities in the hub, peddling everything from luxury items to local specialties.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info12004 = "Commodities of Lumopolis: In addition, rare and exotic imports can also be found here, such as spices and ingredients from faraway lands.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info12101 = "Lumo Knight Responsibilities: Affiliated with the military branch of Lumopolis, the main purpose of Lumo Knights is to repel high-level Eclipsite attacks and search for the remains of ancient civilizations.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info12102 = "Lower Lumopolis Slums: The slums of Lower Lumopolis are the most unsightly blemish upon the city's grandeur. There, the dilapidated stone buildings are mostly abandoned, and the streets are gray and filled with trash, lacking as they are in routine maintenance. Residents of the slums wrap themselves in whatever threadbare garments they can find.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info12103 = "Peace Officers: Guards are entrusted with maintaining law and order in Lumopolis, as well as protecting the Schwartz Family.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info12104 = "Civilian Life in Lumopolis: The majority of the city's civilians are concentrated in Lower Lumopolis, where they not only go for work but also pass the time in its bars, cafes, shops, and theaters.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info12201 = "Lumo Knight Responsibilities: Under regular circumstances, their daily duties also include maintaining law and order in the city.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info12202 = "Lower Lumopolis Slums: Though law and order hardly exist in this place, hopelessness keeps most unrest at bay. It seems even the sunlight has turned away from this sector of the city, letting it shiver and decay in the dark.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info12203 = "Peace Officers: The Guards are divided into several smaller groups, each of which is tasked with defending a different city area. For example, those assigned to protecting the Lumopolis Gardens are known as Lumo Gardens Guards. Likewise, those assigned to the general preservation of peace and order are known as Peace Officers.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info12204 = "Civilian Life in Lumopolis: Most of the citizens hold little to no hope of reaching the heights of their noble counterparts, they prefer to indulge in simpler, less-expensive pastimes.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info12301 = "The Darkover Crisis: The Darkover Crisis began seventeen years ago when the organization known as Eclipse sought to capture the Colossi, gargantuan, advanced flying machines from a long-lost civilization. With an army of Eclipsites in tow, they laid siege to Eraveil, home of the Caelestite race. Very few survivors were left in the wake of their genocide. Finally, seven years later, the Eclipsite army was ultimately routed by the combined military might of Astra, and the Darkover Crisis was brought to an end.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info12302 = "Statue of Queen Bethlehem: The residents of Northland are sincerely fond of their queen. Given the relatively slow pace of life in the north, the dexterous Aurorians of Northland lend much of their free time to the carving of various wooden crafts. Carvings made in the image of Queen Bethlehem are the most common of these sights.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info12303 = "Lumowhistler: A simple piece of candy, especially beloved by small children, that makes a whistling sound when blown upon. For many Aurorians, it is a thing of great nostalgic value. Even adults will sometimes purchase them to recall memories of their childhood.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info12304 = "Crunchy Munchy Crunch: A famous specialty snack from the desert regions of Astra, its appearance can be slightly off-putting for outsiders, but therein lies its appeal. Made from small lizards that have been fried and air-dried to a crisp, they completely retain their original form from when they were alive. A bit gruesome, but perhaps this is part of the desert folks' sense of humor?",
  str_aircraft_tactic_pic_name1 = "Journey's Dawn",
  str_aircraft_tactic_pic_name2 = "Snowland Ballad",
  str_aircraft_tactic_pic_name3 = "Rosa and M&M's Correspondence",
  str_aircraft_tactic_pic_name4 = "Mrs. Red Mercury",
  str_aircraft_tactic_locked_condition = "Unlock 4 clues to obtain!",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info21101 = "Elders: Lords and elders are appointed to rule over small villages and townships, and in some cases, the villagers govern their settlement together. However, all villages and towns must obey the rulings of the Northland royal family regarding major matters.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info21102 = "Canned Herring: A unique food item from Northland that can be stored for a long time. It is very popular with the locals, but outsiders generally find the smell and taste to be too rich.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info21103 = "Gummies: Northland is home to many wild berry varieties, and the soft gummy candy they're creating is a favorite of children across the land.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info21104 = "Fermented Shark Meat: For an unknown reason, sharks have mutated and appeared in the cold Northland water. And the meat can be safely eaten after a specialized fermentation process.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info22101 = "Thatched Hut: a building used for storing grain and wood. Though simple in shape, it is actually relatively windproof.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info22102 = "Northland Population Migration: Many Northland youths leave this cold, backward land and venture into the outside world. However, the unique charm of the north always manages to bring these youngsters back home. You can often see the figure of a traveler returning home on the road to Northland.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info22103 = "Northland's Unique Climate: Most of Northland is covered by ice and snow that remains frozen all year round. Only a few places have a mild climate, with the faint scent of early spring lingering in the snow.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info22104 = "Mountains of Northland: Northland is located by the World's Spine—the highest mountain range on the continent. It is said that you can reach the Land of Eternal Night through this mountain, but this rumor remains a legend. The residents of Northland rarely journey deep into the World's Spine, for the respect and fear of many dangers hidden within the mountain range.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info23101 = "Northland Housing Materials: The building materials used in Northland are relatively basic and essentially consist of roughly processed raw minerals and wood. However, this does not mean that Northland houses lack aesthetic value—in fact, their natural style is seen as an example of pure, unadulterated beauty.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info23102 = "Northland Architecture: The buildings of Northland are commonly built tall and narrow, with high, slender columns. The height and span of their peaks are not limited and can be built as large and high as desired.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info23103 = "Northland Housing Construction: Builders ordinarily use carriages to transport wood for construction purposes, sometimes assisted by Luminatics. For example, they might use ice to form a frame or Lumina to cut through stone.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info23104 = "Landforms of Northland: Northland is surrounded by forests that serve as both a natural barrier and an inexhaustible wellspring of natural resources.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info24101 = "Sawdust Buns: Food rations formulated in response to the war outbreak and have been issued to the soldiers to the present day. The buns taste rather odd, but they are strangely filling and provide adequate nutrition for the common soldiers. The Illumina Federation often refers to these rations as \"Sawdust Buns\" because it is suspected that they are mixed with various borderline edible impurities similar to sawdust.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info24102 = "Chocolate: Residents of colder regions are naturally more accustomed to preserved desserts, so chocolate, with its mellow and sweet flavor, has become one of the few imported products to have gained popularity in Northland.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info24103 = "Northland Livestock: The people of Northland rear docile animals, such as deer, sheep, and poultry. However, certain fierce beasts often appear on their menus, such as brown bears and wild boars, which can only be conquered by hunters.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info24104 = "Fishing: The coastal regions of Northland are ideal for fishing, as are the inland areas along its rivers and lakes. The Aurorians of Northland do not hunt in Lake Mirror, as it is regarded as a sacred region due to centuries of legends and tradition.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info25101 = "Salt: Basic edible salt refined from the Northland sea by villagers of the region. Excess salt is exchanged for miscellaneous items through trade. Generally speaking, the locals use less salt than those in other regions, as they are closer to the sea and can supplement their salt intake with sea fish.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info25102 = "Salt Distribution: Salt sales are relatively minimal in Northland. It is very convenient for residents living by the shore to procure salt, but they don't particularly like to use it in their cooking, as the ingredients gleaned from the sea have enough flavor. Those living inland have a higher demand for salt, but the supply channels of Northland are comparatively underdeveloped, meaning that people often have to go to the seaside to purchase their salt.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info25103 = "Saltwater Lake: There are several large saltwater lakes in Northland. Scholars have determined that these lakes were, in fact, abandoned seas remolded due to changes in the structure of the ancient continent.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info25104 = "Snow Wolves: These ferocious predators of Northland live in packs and seem to possess wisdom that surpasses common beasts.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info26101 = "Pine Frost Valley: One of the regions leading out of Northland. A post guard was built here to defend against Eclipsite invaders.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info26102 = "Wonder Village: This village on the Northland border has a relatively large population and has reached the size of a small town.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info26103 = "Northland Pine: This hill holds a great deal of untapped crystals. The villagers are divided into several manors, large and small, scattered across the flat area between the hills.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info26104 = "Windward Forest: Located in the south of Northland, this forest boasts a warm climate all year round, and is home to many plants and animals.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info27101 = "Luminatics in Northland: Aurorians in Northland espouse the importance of nature in all things by understanding the most fundamental Lumina processes facilitated by nature, resonating with natural entities, and interfering with the world through the realms of imagination and mental perception.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info27102 = "Northland Luminatics Mediums: Luminatics often requires a purely natural medium for Aurorians in Northland. The most common mediums are tools made from tree branches, and some Aurorians can channel animals. Compared to the ceremonies of Lumopolis, the Luminatics of Northland are more primitive, creating a more basic effect, but an effect often more powerful nonetheless.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info27103 = "Northland Faith: Northlanders believe that everything possesses a soul, and that everything can be communicated with—be it an animal, plant, environment, or even a phenomenon.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info27104 = "Faith and Governance: Faith in Northland does not follow a strict organizational structure, and as such, does not have any impact on the rule of the royal family. In fact, the governance of the Northland royal family has always been relatively detached from religion, forming a unique structure almost parallel to popular belief systems.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info28101 = "Luminatics in Illumina: The Luminatics used by the Illumina Federation are different from those used elsewhere and focus more on engineering—by using mechanical mediums developed through technology, practitioners can cast spells without having to hone their minds.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info28102 = "Sled Dogs: Northland residents often rear this breed of dog. They are proficient at pulling sleds, and accompany their owners when hunting. They are even a popular choice when it comes to selecting a pet.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info28103 = "Daily Life in Northland: Daily lives for Northlanders are almost identical. Work begins at sunrise and ends at sunset, and everyone has their duties to attend to, be it farming, animal husbandry, hunting, or manual labor. The elderly often take care of the young at home and impart all the knowledge they possess.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info28104 = "Manual Transportation: The most common form of transportation in Northland is manual. Fortunately, many Aurorians can use Luminatics to assist them in this.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info29101 = "Festival Gatherings: The residents of Northland live simple lives, free from desire. On most days, they rarely seek entertainment and seldom engage in social activities, and it is only during festivals that everyone gets together and shares all the interesting things that they have been doing recently.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info29102 = "Social Activities: During festivals, such as the New Year, people like to sit around and chat, sing, have a storytelling competition, or go for picnics in the nearby forests. The menfolk often organize hunting parties.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info29103 = "Specialty Foods: The specialties of Northland mainly consist of desserts, usually served by the royal family when entertaining guests. In addition, there will be a variety of seafood on the table, such as roast seal and fermented shark meat.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info29104 = "Alcohol: Local alcoholic beverages include honey wine and gin, and the names of these drinks often incorporate ice and snow features.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info30101 = "Closed Borders: Though Northland has recently engaged in trade with other city-states, it remains relatively shut off from the world. Many people living in Northland's inland villages and towns rarely get the chance to meet outsiders, so they welcome visitors heartily and are eager to hear news about the outside world. Because of this, people see the natives of Northland as being warm and hospitable.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info30102 = "Northland Temperament: The people of Northland are simple and pure in character, due to years of isolation and self-sufficiency, but they can also be stubborn and unwilling to accept change. For example, this fear of new ideas makes it difficult for them to adapt to the fast-paced and commercially oriented lifestyle of a place like Umbraton.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info30103 = "Magical Awareness: The people of Northland are not easily surprised by things and events that defy common sense and are even used to such phenomena. For example, when encountering a talking deer, a Northlander would talk to it normally without questioning the bizarre occurrence.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info30104 = "Northland Trade: Northland is adjacent to the sea, so ships dock at its ports regularly, bringing exotic imported goods. However, the residents of Northland are not interested in luxury goods, so merchants will often want to leave Northland as quickly as possible to visit the other city-states of Astra.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info31101 = "Search Parties: The villages of Northland organize search parties when a need arises—for tracking invading Eclipsites, searching for missing Aurorians, and other essential matters. The size of these search parties is unfixed, and they will usually consist of members of four to six. The scope of these parties is generally centered around villages, though they may also focus on areas where Eclipsites have been sighted. The elders request all adult men to assist, and hunters or those familiar with the wilderness are charged with leading the way.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info31102 = "Northland Education: Northland does not have its own standardized education system, and essentially all knowledge is passed on orally.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info31103 = "Northland Law: There is no written law in Northland, and justice usually relies on the spontaneous morality of the villagers when interacting with one another. Local lords or ruling institutions may also be called upon to mediate disputes.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info31104 = "Northland Governance: Northlanders dislike outsiders interfering in the management of their settlements. Because every village and town has its own unique and long history of up to thousands of years, they believe their current practices are adequate.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info32101 = "The Legend of Northland: It is said that the original Aurorians hailed from Northland, and that they bathed in the light of the Aurora and gained great power from it. The Aurorians of Northland hold a deep connection to their land, and irrespective of the great changes in the outside world, they will always see their home as the first and last pure land.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info32102 = "Present Day Northland: As its borders have gradually begun to open up, Northland has become known to an increasing number of outsiders. Even residents of the Rediesel Desert have heard rumors about this place. Other city-states on the continent occasionally receive Northland natives traveling abroad and welcome any opportunity to buy all manner of goods originating from Northland. However, Northland's long period of isolation has cast a veil of ambiguity over the land, and especially in the eyes of ordinary people, Northland remains a mysterious place associated with all kinds of magic and secrecy.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info32103 = "Northland Ruler: At present, Bethlehem is the only member of the Northland royal family. She has become the sole ruler in the hearts of the Northland people by her powerful Luminatics and noble blood. All Northlanders have great respect for Bethlehem, and no one would dream of disobeying her orders or questioning her decisions.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info32104 = "Northland Royal Family: The Northland royal family is the sworn ruler and guardian of Northland. The royal family possesses incomparable power handed down from generation to generation, and has ruled for thousands of years.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info33101 = "Northland Books: Books are rare in Northland, and knowledge is passed on orally, or through carvings, tying knots in ropes, and wooden tablets. Even if there is any, they are made of parchment.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info33102 = "Furniture: Northland has its own interior decoration style based on simplicity over lavishness. Though modest, this style achieves aesthetic elegance through the arrangement and placement of objects.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info33103 = "Music: Music in Northland is mainly enjoyed by children, so the region's musical style is lighthearted and fast, making it very suitable for accompanying fairy tales.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info33104 = "Northland Military: Northland does not have a standing army. Because this remote region does not involve itself in the affairs of the city-states of Astra, each settlement has its own individually established defensive militia of usually no more than a thousand soldiers.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40101 = "Correspondence between Umbraton and Rediesel Desert: In general, most correspondences are delivered by known and trusted people. Delivery times can vary greatly, but a single trip between the two locations takes approximately one month. By employing the Courier Union's professional services, however, delivery times can be shortened to as little as one week.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40102 = "The Rediesel Wrench: A nomadic band of wanderers and outlaws that call the Rediesel Desert their home. Originally a part of Illumina's Advance Team, they were tasked with surface and Undercity exploration; after the tragic losses they experienced in the Secret Territory, however, they deserted from the Illumina Federation and took refuge in the Rediesel Desert. Over time, they slowly became the itinerant bandits that they are known as today.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40103 = "Rediesel Wrench Culture: Freedom bordering on total anarchy are key traits of Rediesel Wrench culture. Survival is their main goal; anything else just adds flavor to their lives.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40104 = "Order Within the Rediesel Wrench: None.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40201 = "Hovercraft: The main mode of transportation used by Illumina's Advance Team during their explorations. While somewhat lacking in creature comforts, this highly-useful vehicle is capable of traversing a wide variety of difficult terrains. As Illumina places a great importance on exploration and research, the hovercraft serves the Federation well by carrying its Advance Team deep into areas outside the reach of ordinary people.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40202 = "Hovercraft Structure: Based on the design of an ordinary truck, hovercrafts are also outfitted with a durable air cushion, allowing them to hover and traverse a wider variety of terrain types (sand dunes, marshes, etc...).",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40203 = "Hovercraft Operation: Under normal circumstances, the rules for operating a hovercraft are no different than those of a regular truck. When hovering is required, hovercrafts must remain within half a meter off the ground. In addition, as hovercrafts are much less stable while hovering, the transportation of large precision instruments is also prohibited.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40204 = "Locomotive Systems of a Hovercraft: In order to maintain their floating capabilities, hovercrafts use specialized ventilators to replace the air in their cushions periodically. When traveling through desert biomes, a special fan must be installed to dislodge sand and other particulate matter.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40301 = "Sandstorms: Sandstorms are a common, natural occurrence in the Rediesel Desert, and generally occur every 24 to 48 hours. Residents of the desert are accustomed to waiting out storms in sandpits or other temporary shelters, their daily lives generally uninterrupted by the howling wind and sand.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40302 = "Temperature Differences: The majority of the Rediesel Desert sees temperatures in excess of 50°C during the day, with temperatures dropping to around 5°C at night. In the slightly-colder northern reaches of the desert, daytime temperatures can reach up to roughly 40°C, but will plummet below 0°C at night.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40303 = "Aurorian Desert Settlements: The vast majority of Aurorians residing in the Rediesel Desert do so in the town of Oasis, with a few choosing to live in the desert's borderlands. Though these nomadic desert-dwellers travel across the sands year-round, they are still limited in their choices by the scarcity of water.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40304 = "Protective Measures: Each household has its own underground \"sand nest\" for taking shelter from the sandstorms. Furniture, equipment, and other belongings are generally wrapped in plastic bags or fabrics to grant them some measure of protection from the sun and the sand.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40401 = "Second-hand Shops: Shops full of wonder and magic that dot the desert's landscape. One never knows what awaits them inside: perhaps their greatest wish, or maybe an unexpected surprise?",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40402 = "Desert Imports: One man's trash is another man's treasure, and second-hand shops are no strangers when it comes to finding these \"treasures.\" All manner of valuable goods can be found lying in junkyards or scattered across the wasteland. Sometimes, the value of these kinds of treasures can only be ascertained by people's willingness to buy them.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40403 = "Low-cost Leftovers: The members of the Rediesel Wrench often stumble across strange and peculiar goods, and are just as prone to selling those goods to second-hand shops if they have no use for them. Naturally, these shops also serve as pawn shops for the other inhabitants of the desert.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40404 = "Do-it-Yourself: Second-hand shops are notorious for reconstructing or even modifying their finds with bits and pieces lying around their workshops. Naturally, these contraptions fail to meet the standards of their original manufacturers, but are nonetheless useful in a hostile and unpredictable place like the Rediesel Desert.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40501 = "Formation of Desert Gangs: Itinerant residents of the Rediesel Desert make up a large amount of its bandit gangs. While they generally spend their days scouring the desert for valuables, they are also known to ambush travelers and even band together to raid Illumina's military caravans.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40502 = "Style of Banditry: Desert gangs generally prey on the weak while cowering from the strong. They have no guidelines or scruples, much less morals, and are unabashedly selfish in thought and action.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40503 = "Bandits and the Rediesel Wrench: The majority of desert gangs and bandits have come to fear the Rediesel Wrench, namely because they are the ones that punish them for their banditry. Oftentimes, just the sight of the Rediesel Wrench will make entire gangs turn tail and retreat into the sands.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40504 = "Tech Fragments: These shards of technology are often dug up all throughout the Rediesel Desert. While no one is certain of their origins or purpose, everyone is certain of one thing: they always fetch a handsome price in the market.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40601 = "Lumopolis Day: Lumopolis Day is a holiday that celebrates the establishment of the city of Lumopolis. The celebration displays the strength of Lumopolis to the world, and instills a sense of honor in its citizens. Only the most luxurious of decorations are used for the celebration, a conspicuous nod to the city's vast wealth. Foreign dignitaries and other important guests are often invited to take part in the festivities, which culminate in a sumptuous feast.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40602 = "Lumopolis Day Snacks: During the festivities, the streets of Lumopolis are packed with snack stalls, which offer all of their wares free of charge. The citizens of Lumopolis will provide home-baked fruit pies and other delectable treats for the grand celebration.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40603 = "Lumopolis Day - Entry/Exit Regulations: During the festivities, entry and exit regulations are loosened in order to allow more foreigners to take part in the celebration. Visitors need not worry about expenses during this holiday, as most goods and services are offered for free on Lumopolis Day.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40604 = "The Silent Banquet: A very unique auction held in Umbraton. On the surface, it appears no different than any other banquet, with guests enjoying the finest dishes and entertainment the city has to offer. However, during this special feast, all manner of staggeringly-priced transactions are known to occur, all without the slightest word being spoken...",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40701 = "Music Genres: Different regions enjoy varying music styles that better suit their individual and cultural tastes. While the prevailing music of Lumopolis is elegant and refined, the music enjoyed in the Rediesel Desert is pulsing with energy and enthusiasm. Music in Northland is simple yet lively, while the music of the Illumina Federation is more somber and reserved...",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40702 = "Instruments: Instruments are inseparably related to the preferred music styles of a region. Violins, pianos, and organs dominate the musical landscape of Lumopolis, while electric guitars, bass guitars, and drum sets are a common and welcome sight in the Rediesel Desert's pubs. Woodwind instruments are household items for residents of Northland, while brass instruments are preferred in the Illumina Federation.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40703 = "Musicians: Lumopolis boasts the highest concentration of famous musicians, possibly because many consider the violin and piano to be the most elegant of instruments. Younger citizens, on the other hand, are more drawn to guitars and drums than the more \"refined\" options.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40704 = "Musical Education: While many schools offer curricula that involve music to a certain degree, there is no professional music academy for aspiring musicians. As a result, those who wish to make a career out of music would do better to seek tutelage from established, successful performers.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40801 = "Illumina Convoys: Each Illumina convoy is composed of two to four cargo trucks, each requiring two drivers. In addition, a minimum of three sidecar motorcycles are assigned as security escorts for each truck.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40802 = "Convoy Transport Routes: Convoys are generally responsible for the transportation of goods between the various Undercities. Due to the physical limitations of convoy trucks, relatively-wide roads are selected as transport routes; only a small number of convoys transport goods outside of these established trade routes.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40803 = "Means of Transportation: The Gaz truck is the Illumina Federation's preferred vehicle for industrial transportation. Powerful, efficient, and easy to mass produce, this hulking truck is considered somewhat \"ugly\" in terms of its aesthetics; nevertheless, its utility and practicality cannot be denied.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40804 = "Transported Goods: The Illumina Federation's convoys generally transport mined ores, components manufactured in Gannon, and everyday necessities. In addition, the convoys are often tasked with the transportation of military arms, though the specifics are kept hidden from outsiders.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40901 = "Marriage in Umbraton: Marriages in Umbraton are relatively unregulated, and do not require any form of certification. For members of different crime syndicates, the approval of the boss is generally required; for ordinary citizens, parental approval from both parties more than suffices.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40902 = "Umbraton Weddings: Weddings are often grandiose occasions in Umbraton, with the parents of the newlyweds offering expensive gifts in their honor as a symbol of their approval of their matrimony.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40903 = "Floral Gates: Gates that have been elaborately decorated with flowers for an Umbraton wedding; crossing these floral thresholds together symbolizes the start of a couple's eternal union. To a certain extent, the beauty and detail of these gates indicates the future happiness of the newlyweds; naturally, choosing the right language of flowers is immensely important.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info40904 = "Selection Criteria: The most common (and oftentimes most important) criteria when seeking a partner in Umbraton is financial stability, a natural choice in a hyper-commercialized society. When asking the question of which is more important, money or love, it is good to remember that in Umbraton, money can buy even the sweetest love; love, on the other hand, does not necessarily put food on the table.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info41001 = "Rediesel: A crimson-colored material commonly used in paint. Primarily produced in the Rediesel Desert, where a great many things are also painted red (mostly due to the lack of other colors).",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info41002 = "Sandworms: A common food item in the desert. When fried, their taste and texture are quite enjoyable, and they are easy to store for future consumption. Never underestimate the value of these critters, as they are jam-packed with nutrients, and can even taste like chicken if properly prepared!",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info41003 = "Lizards: A common food item in the desert. Generally air-dried prior to cooking, their meat is chewy and savory, and their skins are usually tanned to make leather goods. The quality of these lizard-hide goods is especially sought after by a number of outsiders.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info41004 = "Cactus: A rarely-seen desert plant that is often used to make special beverages. While its water content is laughably low, its rich aroma is known to entice the otherwise carnivorous denizens of the desert. Some even claim that drinks made using cacti can strengthen the body and beautify the skin.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info41101 = "Communication in the Rediesel Desert (1): There is no established telecommunications system in the Rediesel Desert, and most information is conveyed person-to-person. As a result, residents of the desert are often far behind the rest of the world in terms of information; in some cases, there are people who have never even heard of Lumopolis!",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info41102 = "Communication in the Rediesel Desert (2): Following the introduction of basic technological products from the Illumina Federation, larger desert settlements began using radios and handheld transceivers to communicate. Though different channels were established for communication, they are often used interchangeably and thus are subject to frequent interference.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info41103 = "Eclipsites in the Rediesel Desert: A large number of Eclipsites roam the northern and western parts of the desert, while encounters in the southern and eastern parts are few and far between. Regardless of location, the inhabitants of the Rediesel Deserts rely on experience and caution to avoid Eclipsite confrontations as much as possible.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info41104 = "Eclipsite Defenses: Larger desert settlements will often construct basic defensive structures, such as scrap-metal walls and ramparts, to protect themselves from the Eclipsite menace. Smaller settlements and solitary travelers, on the other hand, have little choice but to flee for their lives.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info41201 = "Umbraton: Umbraton is the conglomeration of towns located directly beneath the floating island of Azurite. Situated in the central plains of Astra, its location is perfect for ground transportation as well as for accessing the continent's most prosperous trade center: Lumopolis.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info41202 = "Umbraton's Origins: Originally, Umbraton was designated as the slum sector of Lumopolis, and was under the sheriff's direct authority. As it grew in size and population, however, governance over Umbraton grew more and more unstable, until it finally established itself as its own domain. Now, Umbraton is governed entirely by its local merchant guilds, as well as various competing gangs and syndicates.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info41203 = "Umbraton's Architecture: While most of Umbraton is comprised of shoddy, dense, and disorganized houses, more well-constructed and decorative buildings can be found in the city center. Many of these buildings are the headquarters of Umbraton's many guilds, as well as venues of entertainment, such as bars and casinos.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info41204 = "Contempt for the Military: Prior to the Darkover Crisis, Umbraton had never been the target of a single Eclipsite attack; as a result, the city attached very little importance to military affairs. After all, in a hyper-commercialized society where wealth decides everything, what good is a powerful army if it fails to make any money?",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info41301 = "Organizational Structure of the Rediesel Wrench: The Rediesel Wrench is divided into numerous, smaller teams, each of which operates under its own rules; the leaders of each team, in turn, follow and obey the orders of the Rediesel Wrench's leader. Leadership of the Rediesel Wrench is determined through a rite of succession in which the next leader inherits \"the Wrench\", a symbol of authority within the organization.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info41302 = "\"Rediesel-style\" Entertainment: The members of the Rediesel Wrench live to plunder, and plunder to live; to them, nothing is more exciting or enjoyable than carrying out a thrilling and dangerous robbery. It is said that, in some instances, certain members of the gang have actually returned the stolen goods to their rightful owners, claiming that they simply enjoy the thrill of looting more than the loot itself.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info41303 = "Umbraton Culture: Umbraton maintains a free and open-minded attitude towards people of all races and backgrounds. Anyone can find success in Umbraton, so long as they have the brains and the will to succeed; as a result, countless industries have cropped up all across the city, offering everything a person could need for the right price.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info41304 = "Umbraton Laws: There are few written laws in Umbraton, as order is largely maintained through the power of its various gangs and syndicates. In essence, so long as people do not violate the few principles laid forth by the powers that be (or get caught doing so), anything constitutes as \"fair play.\" As a result, most people in Umbraton prefer to handle their business under the cover of night.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50101 = "The origin of the Underground Arena: The Underground Arena in Umbraton was formerly known as the Pit, which was a popular form of entertainment among Lumo nobles. The thrilling fights that took place there also attracted a large audience from the general population, and it gradually evolved into a way to settle disputes between the various forces in Umbraton.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50102 = "The rules of the Underground Arena: Fights are generally held from 8 p.m. to 6 a.m. Teams of five fight each other in pairs. There are no restrictions, and the method of determining the winner is brutal and straightforward: if one of the teams surrenders or is unable to fight, the team loses.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50103 = "Underground Arena rewards: There were no grand champions in these matches, only the title of Midnight Champion. The team with the most points and no losses on any given night would retain the champion's belt until the following night. Naturally, any team that could retain the title for multiple nights would be the object of respect, as well as jealousy.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50104 = "Changes in the Underground Arena: The Underground Arena of the early days was chaotic and dangerous, as various forces often used it as a way to settle disputes. When Istvan became the Shadowlord, he created the following three rules: 1. No killing of opponents. 2. No one could send more than one team. 3. If anyone wished to dispute the result of a match, they must raise their objection at the moment and not at some later time.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50201 = "Lumopolis' governance of Umbraton: If Lumopolis had ever managed Umbraton, it was to collect taxes. The nobles never cared about what Umbraton would become, only how much money they could squeeze out of it. As a result, the sheriffs and tax collectors assigned to Umbraton were soon in cahoots with the gangs and guilds here, and degenerated into slaves of Umbraton's money.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50202 = "Business safety in Umbraton: The one rule in Umbraton is that there are no rules. Perhaps you could call this freedom. Therefore, in order to ensure their safety, large guilds often form private armed forces. Smaller guilds will pool their resources in joint ventures to recruit mercenaries, and individual traders usually pay protection fees to a gang or one of the guilds.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50203 = "The Gangs of Umbraton: Nobles exiled from Lumopolis tend to continue to structure their lives in Umbraton around family, while deserters of the Illumina Federation retain the hierarchical structures they were used to. The different local gangs, meanwhile, greet each other with slang and street speak. Umbraton welcomes and accommodates everyone.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50204 = "Dark industries: In the various alleys of Umbraton, buyers can find anything they want—arms from Illumina Federation, household goods from the Lumo nobles, and even Eclipsites... Do not ask where they come from.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50301 = "The weapons industry in Umbraton: Rifles, ammunition, and officers' service pistols from Illumina, soldiers' armor and shields from Lumopolis, and even long swords with the heraldries of noble families can all be found in Umbraton... as long as the buyer can afford the price.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50302 = "Legal businesses: If you want to buy weapons in Umbraton, it's wise not to ask too many questions about where they came from. Any Umbraton businessman will tell you that their goods are legal, but that statement should be taken with a grain of salt.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50303 = "Arms resale: As a major distribution center for groups looking to flip wares at a profit, the weapons in Umbraton are sold in private. Buyers willing to pay the price can also issue secret commissions, and someone in Umbraton will be able to get a hold of what they are looking for.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50304 = "Side gig economy: To avoid unnecessary complications, none of the guilds or individuals claim to be arms dealers. However, buyers can get arms from any person or guild if they can just find the right place to announce a reasonable offer. This is the duality of professionalism and side gigs in Umbraton.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50401 = "Excerpts from Lumopolis wedding customs: In general, marriage in Lumopolis is relatively feudal in nature, especially when it comes to marriage between classes. First, nobles and commoners are not allowed to intermarry. Second, both parties to a marriage must have the consent of their families or parents. Third, they practice monogamy, and spouses must remain faithful to each other.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50402 = "Marriage under the God of Light: Weddings must be performed in the temple of the God of Light, with a priest as a witness. If these requirements are not met, the marriage will not be protected and blessed. Infidelity to one's spouse is absolutely forbidden, and perpetrators of this crime are put to trial, with punishments ranging from deprivation of peerage to death.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50403 = "Consequences of violation: Nobles who marry commoners out of love are exiled and become commoners. If they are clergy, they are excommunicated.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50404 = "Marriage in the temple: Those who have taken a lifelong vow to serve the God of Light, such as the priests, will lose all connection with worldly life, while those who serve the temple, such as knights, are not held to strict requirements by the God of Light.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50501 = "The process of visiting Lumopolis: Except for some extraordinary people, it is almost impossible for commoners to enter Lumopolis. Ordinary people can find various ways into Umbraton, which are naturally expensive and require much patience because one will have to endure the long wait for vetting in the transit zone.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50502 = "Transit Zone: Originally a transportation depot placed between Umbraton and Lumopolis, it gradually formed into a transit zone due to the many caravans staying there. In this place, Lumopolis conducts preliminary vetting on the caravans and personnel before they enter the city.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50503 = "Lumopolis' Vetting: Entering Lumopolis is not an easy task, as people have to go through a long and tedious identity check before being granted access. Of course, if one has a letter of introduction with an aristocratic family's emblem, the waiting time can be significantly reduced.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50504 = "Dense housing: People's first impression of the transit zone is usually that its layout is much like that of Umbraton: a large number of houses, densely packed together in a disorderly manner. This is because the houses here were originally built to facilitate quick access to the former transport station. The high density also makes the place easier to defend against the harassment from the wilderness, bringing a sense of security to the occupants. ",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50601 = "People waiting: People's reasons for entering Lumopolis vary widely from visiting family and friends to business, tourism, or just getting a good look at the great temple of the God of Light. The wait is long and tedious, and the row upon row of inns in the transit zone cater to these people.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50602 = "Innkeepers in the transit zone: In order to show how civilized they are, some residents of Lower Lumopolis gather funding to set up inns. There, they can welcome visitors while also showing off the power of Lumopolis to them. Inns franchised by the major clans of Lumopolis only receive guests invited by the family. Other inns are funded by the temple and are exclusive to God of Light's followers. Inns opened by major guilds in Umbraton cater to caravans, but are also open to common passers-by. After all, the people of Umbraton would never let go of any opportunity to make money.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50603 = "Inn Services in the Transit Zone: In addition to the usual meals and accommodation, the inns in the transit zone provide various information to the lodgers. This mainly includes introductions to Lumopolis, including its noble family, celebrities, beliefs, and so on. Naturally, there is also no shortage of well-connected people who can provide relationship-lubricating services for those who can not stand the long vetting process.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50604 = "The View and Price of Houses in the Transit Zone: Due to the highly dense housing, people staying in the transit zone have limited views from their windows. This means that inns that have multiple floors or were situated on good locations and on high ground are expensive. After all, a good view can make life more comfortable while waiting to enter Lumopolis. ",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50701 = "Nobles and Family Emblems: In Lumopolis, family emblems show which family a person belongs to and what their status is in Lumopolis. Although the intricate patterns look like abstruse writing to outsiders, everyone in Lumopolis are familiar with them. After all, they are an essential part of their daily life.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50702 = "The Temple's Emblem: The belief in the God of Light is widespread throughout Lumopolis. With the permission of the temple, believers can wear the emblem of God of Light or embroider it on their clothing to show their devotion to the God of Light.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50703 = "The Formal Attire of Umbraton: Made of precious silk from the east or other precious materials from the continent, the clothes of the people here are flattering, comfortable, and adorned with various accessories. Dark gold and purple are the two favorite tones of people in Umbraton. These colors display another attitude they have towards life—to always remain untamed. ",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50704 = "The Casual Attire of Umbraton: Leather boots and coats, scarves and turbans that cover the whole face—these are the clothes people of Umbraton usually wear. These serve to better conceal their faces and the various weapons they carry.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50801 = "The Laws of Lumopolis: Nobles and commoners are governed by different laws. The status and corresponding powers of one's family grant different rights, as well as certain immunities.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50802 = "Trials in Lumopolis: The Hall of Justice in Lumopolis is generally responsible for adjudication, while the Elder Council handles cases involving nobles. In the latter scenario, the judge would be appointed by the City Lord. The appointment of the Chief Judge requires the unanimous approval of the Elder Council and the temple, which is usually the result of a balancing of power among multiple parties.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50803 = "Punishment in Lumopolis: Commoners and nobles who commit serious crimes are held jointly responsible and are usually executed by sword or hanging. People who commit minor offenses are imprisoned or exiled.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50804 = "The Gallows in Lumopolis: When an execution is going to be carried out, temporary gallows are set up at the square. They usually include upright posts to bind the convicts, a guillotine, and a wooden frame for hanging.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50901 = "Inheritance in Umbraton: Although the people of Umbraton place immense importance on wealth, they can not take it with them when they reach the end of their lives. As is in their nature, most Umbraton people leave their wealth and status to their biological descendants.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50902 = "The Effect of a Will: Umbraton residents who lead solitary lives or for various reasons have no biological relatives will most often draw up a will at the end of their lives. An acquaintance or a reliable gang will then be trusted to handle their property and arrange for the succession of their status.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50903 = "The Role of the Second-in-command: For large guilds, both blood heirs and wills are sometimes subject to accidents, such as the sudden death of an heir or the demise of a principal who has not yet drawn up a will. In most such cases, the second-in-command inherits their position. Naturally, the appointment of the second-in-command also tends to cause various disputes.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info50904 = "The Rulings of the Multitude: Many successions become controversial because of the wealth and status involved, which has been the cause of much bloodshed in Umbraton. It usually ends with one side winning, or more often, with both sides losing, leaving no one to take over. At this point, prominent figures in Umbraton make their appearance to jointly decide how things should be handled. After the Shadowlord took control of the area, people respect his decision in such matters.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info51001 = "Reading Materials: In Umbraton, anyone who can afford it can have their writing printed by a mimeograph machine. Thus, the city flourishes with all kinds of publications, including magazines, periodicals, newspapers, and flyers.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info51002 = "Manuscripts: Commoners in Lumopolis are not allowed to own books, including handwritten copies. Only the mansions of the nobles and the temple keep a large number of manuscripts. This is not only because they are allowed to, but mainly because they can afford to keep many copyists.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info51003 = "Parchment Scrolls: Travelers should not be surprised to see Northlanders with knotted ropes, inscribed wooden tablets, or even small stone tablets with writing carved into them. These are their books. In Northland, where word of mouth is the primary means to pass on messages, reading materials are rare, and only major events are recorded on scrolls made of parchment for safekeeping.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info51004 = "Private Books: If you see some handwritten booklets or scrolls with unrecognizable text, these are most likely the work of some organization that wishes to keep their dealings secret and so uses encrypted text for their documents.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info51101 = "Newspapers in Umbraton: Newspaper reporters always seem busy. After all, newspapers require fresh and new content. For the sake of speed, most large news offices have printing machines of the lowest grade that can print thousands of copies of newspapers as soon as the content is written and typeset. Smaller newspapers often hire specialized drivers to quickly deliver the manuscripts to printing houses. Others who only have a few people working for them use manual printing machines to mimeograph. Naturally, such newspapers are issued in a smaller quantity, and the quality is also relatively poor.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info51102 = "Umbraton's Magazines: Since only printing houses have specialized binders and cover makers, if you want to print a magazine you have to send it to a specialized printing house. However, some magazine publishers also use manual printing machines and non-professional craftsmen to print and bind magazines, resulting in magazines of inferior quality. Consequently, they have to rely on highly novelty-hunting headlines and fast circulation to secure their position in the market. At this point, these magazines are really not that different from newspapers.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info51103 = "Umbraton's Novels: Freedom of speech is the most important ethos in Umbraton. Anyone can publish their work as long as they can afford the cost of printing and distribution. Naturally, if the content is too extreme, printing houses and booksellers will still hesitate over whether they should take the money or go on living.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info51104 = "Knowledge-based Books in Umbraton: Few people show any interest in knowledge-based books due to the pragmatism or even secularism that prevails in Umbraton. Everyone there is busy making money. People who dare to publish such books in Umbraton are either wealthy scholars or have the secret support of some organization.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info51201 = "News in Lumopolis: Due to the different classes of nobles and commoners, there is no public news publication in Lumopolis. Nobles only care about what is happening in the upper circles, where news that the commoners will never hear are spread by word of mouth. Commoners, meanwhile, are only concerned with whatever actions by the nobles or the temple affect their life. They are usually informed on such matters by the announcements of the various administrative officers in Lumopolis. Occasionally, Lumopolis gets information about the outside world when someone brings newspapers from Umbraton.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info51202 = "Lumopolis' Book Collection: Lumopolis' temple has the largest collection of books. Specialized personnel transcribe various books, categorize them, and keep records. The books are kept in their library, which is open only to the temple staff. Nobles also keep small libraries in their homes and arrange a number of rather exclusive book clubs and salons.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info51203 = "The Books of the Temple: Books covering the various treatises on the religion of the God of Light, famous miracles, and the experiences of believers constitute the vast majority of the collection in the Lumopolis temple. Naturally, some liberal-minded monks use their understanding of the God of Light to write fascinating secular stories to make more people to read about and understand the God of Light.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info51204 = "Book Dealers in Lumopolis: At certain times, commoners from Lumopolis appear in Umbraton carrying a pile of money and a stack of manuscripts to be printed and published. Subsidized by nobles or the temple, these book dealers are a bit of an anomaly in Umbraton. They do not seek profits but are more concerned with the print quality and how well the books circulate. After all, in the eyes of these commoners, it is more important to complete the tasks given by the top than to earn money.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info51301 = "The Secret Court of Lumopolis: In Lumopolis Gardens, there is a place where confidential files and archives are kept. It is said that only the City Lord of Lumopolis, essential members of the Elder Council, and representatives of significant noble families have access to it.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info51302 = "The Jewel of Lumopolis: Daybreak Crystal is a rare mineral that is said to be found not in veins but at seemingly random locations, which makes it difficult to find and mine. Even the raw ore emits different colors under different lights and from different angles, while polished stones emit a veritable kaleidoscope of color. Even Lumo Nobles, who have seen countless exotic treasures, can not resist its charm.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info51303 = "Umbraton's Replica Paintings: When the luxury goods of Lumopolis were introduced to Umbraton, they brought not only wealth to the locals but also inspired in them an appreciation for art. Once the people became rich enough to not have to worry about making a living, they started pursuing the art of Lumopolis. And thus, the replication industry born. All kinds of famous oil paintings can be found in Umbraton. They are displayed everywhere, including guilds, cafes, and bars. It's even rumored that the initiation ceremonies of some gangs involve the burning of a painting.",
  str_aircraft_tactic_info51304 = "Umbraton Wariness: Very sensitive to money and territory, small business owners in Umbraton tend to be very careful with their scope of operation and avoid crossing unspoken boundaries. For example, a snack peddler selling in the East End would never do business in the West even if there was demand to be met and more money to be made, because very likely a snack peddler would already be serving the area with paid protection and would have every right to drive away a competitor."
}
return config
